{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Astigmatism Correction}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Astigmatism_Correction}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Astigmatism Correction}
\b\fs36\cf1 Astigmatism Correction
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This panel allows you to \uldb \b correct astigmatism\plain\b\fs24 {\v Astigmatism_Correction@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24  in the image. The astigmatism correction parameters are stored and recalled each time you select Stigmation again. 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-6 \cellx8715\cellx9215\cellx14265\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \ul Click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} on \b Stigmation \plain\fs24 button.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Adjust stigmation correction to remove Astigmatism in image:\plain\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li715\fi-355\tx715 \{bmc bm1.bmp\}\tab \ul Drag\plain\fs24 {\v DRAG@Sem.HLP} with the left mouse button in the Image Window to adjust stigmation in x and y.
\par\intbl or
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Pick up and drag the red point
\par\intbl or
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab use the \ul Scroll Bars\plain\fs24 {\v 2HOSDE@Sem.HLP} to adjust x/y
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Click Mag/Focus\plain\fs24  to activate the mouse to magnification and focus setting in the image plane.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select another tab or close SEM Control with \{bmc bm2.bmp\}
\par\intbl \par\pard \pard\intbl For further information about parameter adjustment refer to \uldb \b Navigation Box\plain\b\fs24 {\v 23WW_9K@Sem.HLP}\cell\pard \pard\intbl \plain\fs24 \cell\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm3.bmp\}\b \cell\intbl\row
\pard\tx355 
\par \plain\fs24 \{bmc bm4.bmp\}\tab  When adjusting stigmation it is generally considered easier to adjust one axis at a time using the navigation box scroll bars, rather than attempting to adjust X and Y stigmation simultaneously which requires more experience.
\par 
\par For additional information see \uldb \b Stigmation Mode\plain\b\fs24 {\v K5RRU4@Sem.HLP}\plain\fs24  and  \uldb \b How to correct astigmatism\plain\b\fs24 {\v Astigmatism_Correction@sem.hlp}\plain\fs24  \b 
\par \page
