\par \pard \plain\fs24 The fundamental noise reduction is chosen by selecting an appropriate \ul \b\ul Scan Speed\plain\b\fs24 {\v scan_speed}\plain\fs24  which defines the basic dwell time of the beam on a pixel
\par 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx7475\cellx12445\pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \b 
\par\intbl \plain\fs24 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \plain\fs24 Select Noise Reduction mode between \ul Frame Average\plain\fs24 {\v Frame_Average_Mode}, \ul Frame Integrate\plain\fs24 {\v Frame_Integrate_Mode}, and \ul Line Average\plain\fs24 {\v Line_Average_Mode} from the \ul Drop-down List\plain\fs24 {\v XYVXW3@Sem.HLP}.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab Select \b Freeze Mode \plain\fs24 from the Drop-down List as \b Command\plain\fs24  which causes an immediate freeze of the current zone (the whole image in normal mode) when the \b Freeze button\plain\fs24  is pressed  or  \b End\plain\fs24  \b Frame\plain\fs24  causes the zone to freeze at the end of the current frame.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Unfreeze\plain\fs24  is used to reset the noise reduction cycle and resume image acquisition.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \{bmc bm0.bmp\}\tab \b Scan + \plain\fs24 button increases scan speed (faster, lower scan speed numbers) and \b Scan -\plain\fs24  button decreases scan speed (slower, higher scan speed numbers)
\par\intbl \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm13.bmp\}\cell\intbl\row
