{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Protected Z}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Protected_Z}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Protected Z
\par \plain\fs24 
\par This SEM parameter controls the behaviour of the stage when a multi axis move is performed (e.g. Go To a position label).
\par 
\par \b Parameter not Set\plain\fs24 .
\par All relevent axes move simultaneously to the desired position.
\par Backlash correction performed if required.
\par 
\par \b Parameter Set
\par \plain\fs24 The move to the desired position is performed in phases to minimise the risk of collision.
\par The parameter \b Safe Z\plain\fs24  defines the maximum Z position to be used while moving in XY. Set this according to the tallest sample you have mounted.
\par \pard 
\par The movement sequence is:
\par 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 If either the desired Z or Safe Z is lower than the current Z then this axis is moved to whichever is the lowest position.
\par If the desired Tilt is lower than the current Tilt then this axis is moved to the desired position
\par The X,Y,R,M axes are moved simultaneously to their desired positions
\par If The desired Tilt position is not yet achieved move Tilt to the desired position
\par If the desired Z position is not yet achieved move Z to the desired position.
\par 
\par 
\par The \b Protected Z\plain\fs24  parameter may only be changed with \ul Supervisor Privilege\plain\fs24 {\v XTAC5O@admin32.hlp}.
\par \page
