{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} SEM Control X-Ray}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} B2XQVU}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 SEM Control X-Ray
\par \pard \plain\fs24 
\par This window provides set up and control for X-Ray dot map input
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx9065\cellx13815\pard\intbl\tx355 
\par\intbl X-Ray dot map inputs are connected to X-Ray ports. At installation these ports are given \b identifiers\plain\fs24  consistent with the X-Ray system in use, these identifiers appear on the left of the window (e.g. WIN1 toWIN7). They may be edited by the user.
\par\intbl Each port supplies the count pulses for a selected energy window. These pulses are accumulated on a pixel basis and used as source information for the Dot Map function.
\par\intbl On entry to the X-Ray setup window the normal mode display LUT contents are stored and the display LUT switched into X-Ray mode.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl There are three parts to the dot map function:
\par\intbl \{bmc bm22.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b setup of the required function\plain\b\fs24 {\v X_Ray_Dot_Map__Function_Setup}\plain\fs24 ,
\par\intbl \{bmc bm22.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b data acquisition\plain\b\fs24 {\v X_Ray_Dot_Map__Start_Acquisition}\plain\fs24  
\par\intbl \{bmc bm22.bmp\}\tab \uldb \b colour coding of the display LUT\plain\b\fs24 {\v X_Ray_Dot_Map__Energy_Window_Setup}\plain\fs24 .
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b Closing\plain\fs24  the X-Ray window will give an \uldb \b X-Ray Reset\plain\b\fs24 {\v X_Ray_Dot_Map__Reset}\plain\fs24  
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b \{bmc bm23.bmp\} Registration of X-Ray data with image:\plain\fs24 \par\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \tab Different X-Ray systems may have different internal timings which may give rise to a slight mismatch in registration between the X-Ray data and the image. If this is found to be the case reducing the data acquisition scan rate will reduce the mismatch. It may be necessary to experiment to find the fastest acquisition rate which gives a suitable registration where high accuracy is required. \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li355\fi-355\tx355 \pard\intbl\tx355 \par\pard \pard\intbl\tx355 To obtain additional information point to the area in the picture. When the cursor changes from \{bmc bm24.bmp\}to \{bmc bm25.bmp\}\ul click\plain\fs24 {\v CLICK@Sem.HLP} to present the additional information.\par\pard \pard\intbl \{bmc bm26.shg\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
