{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Survey Mode State}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Survey_Mode}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn \b\fs36\cf1 Survey Mode State
\par \pard \plain\fs24 Survey Mode state is first entered when Survey Mode is switched On (either via the \uldb \b Settings Dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Settings_Dialog}\plain\fs24 ) or by switching the Survey Mode Parameter.
\par 
\par It is also entered from \uldb \b Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode}\plain\fs24  when\b  <F4>\plain\fs24  is pressed
\par 
\par On entry to Survey Mode State from the OFF state the current Magnification, Working Distance, Stage Z and Brightness are saved for use when Survey Mode is switched off.
\par 
\par On entering Survey mode state the Magnification is set either to the defined magnification or to the lowest achievable magnification for the conditions. The working distance is set to the defined Working Distance (constrained to the Maximum achievable Working Distance and the Low User Z limit ).
\par \pard 
\par The brightness is set to the value last used in Survey Mode State.
\par 
\par If required a Fine Auto Focus is next executed followed by the Survey Mode Macro if defined.
\par 
\par \page
