{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard {\up K}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up K} Go To Previous Point;Goto First Position;Input LUT;Joystick Disable;Label Position;Limits;List Clear;List Load;List SaveAs;Mark Position;Move XY Only;Noise Reduction;Optibeam;Position List;Preparations for using Survey Mode;Protected Z;Record;Resolution Mode State;SEM Control Apertures;SEM Control Detectors;SEM Control Gun;Track Z}
\b\fs36\cf1 Preparations for using Survey Mode.
\par \plain\fs24 
\par Survey Mode may only be used when the Stage is initialised and Optibeam is switched on. 
\par See \uldb \b SEM Control Apertures\plain\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Control_Apertures}\plain\fs24 .
\par 
\par Using the \uldb \b Settings dialog\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Settings_Dialog}\plain\fs24  define the conditions for\uldb \b  Survey Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Survey_Mode}\plain\fs24 , \uldb \b Resolution Mode State\plain\b\fs24 {\v Resolution_Mode}\plain\fs24  and, if required, the Exit Macro.
\par 
\par Ensure that the \uldb \b Stage Z High and Low user limits\plain\b\fs24 {\v HE_C4L@dlgmgr.hlp}\plain\fs24  are correctly set for the specimen to be reviewed, in particular the High limit to prevent collision with the Final lens. (Right button click on the background of the \uldb \b SEM Control Stage\plain\b\fs24 {\v SEM_Control_Stage}\plain\fs24  Tab and select \b Limits...\plain\fs24 ).
\par \pard 
\par Obtain a focussed image under your normal (Survey Mode OFF) conditions.
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Frame Integrate (Scan Speed)}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Frame_Integrate__Scan_Speed_}
{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard \b\fs36\cf1 Frame Integrate Mode
\par \plain\fs24 
\par \pard\li355\fi-355\tx355 The \uldb \b scan speed\plain\b\fs24 {\v scan_speed}\plain\fs24  defines the time to complete a frame and the Noise reduction parameter\b  N\plain\fs24  defines the number of frames to integrate.
\par 
\par The image automatically freezes at the end of the integration cycle.
\par \page
